{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" of PostHog’s batch capture API, so an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"can send events to PostHog Cloud or a self-hosted PostHog’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"POST \/batch\/"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","type":"conformsTo","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"title":"Conforms To"}],"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogBatchEncoder\/init(projectToken:plan:limit:)"],"title":"Initializers","generated":true},{"anchor":"Instance-Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)"],"title":"Instance Methods","generated":true},{"anchor":"Type-Aliases","identifiers":["doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogBatchEncoder\/Failure"],"title":"Type Aliases","generated":true},{"anchor":"Type-Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogBatchEncoder\/batchLimit"],"title":"Type Properties","generated":true}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"PostHogBatchEncoder"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"overview","text":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Make the destination with "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/postHog(projectToken:host:plan:backoff:clock:)"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which fills in the endpoint, this encoder and PostHog’s limits:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let postHog = try HTTPDestination.postHog(","    projectToken: projectToken,","    host: postHogHost,  \/\/ https:\/\/eu.i.posthog.com","    plan: plan)"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The body is a JSON object of content type "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"application\/json"},{"type":"text","text":" with two members: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"api_key"},{"type":"text","text":", the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"project token, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"batch"},{"type":"text","text":", one object per record, oldest first, with these members:"}]},{"type":"table","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Member","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Holds"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"distinct_id"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The record’s session, its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SessionKey"},{"type":"text","text":", as a lowercase UUID string; the record’s own "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EventRecord\/id"},{"type":"text","text":" when its context has no session"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"event","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The event’s "},{"code":"Event\/name","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", as it is"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"properties","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The event’s stored properties, by name, then the members listed below","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"timestamp","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When the event was tracked: ISO 8601 in UTC, with milliseconds ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"2026-11-23T14:03:27.512Z"},{"type":"text","text":")"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"uuid"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The record’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EventRecord\/id"},{"text":", as a lowercase UUID string; a redelivered record keeps it","type":"text"}]}]]],"header":"row"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The session is the only identifier sent, and every event is anonymous: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"properties"},{"type":"text","text":" holds"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$process_person_profile: false"},{"type":"text","text":", so PostHog makes no person profile, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$geoip_disable: true"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"so PostHog doesn’t add a location from the request’s IP address. A record with no session (one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tracked by a tracker without "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Enricher.sessions()"},{"type":"text","text":", or one a store recovered after a relaunch,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which keeps no context) is its own anonymous person, linked to nothing: PostHog rejects a whole"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"batch when one of its events has no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"distinct_id"},{"type":"text","text":". PostHog counts a person per "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"distinct_id"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"so its unique users are sessions. The session is also sent as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$session_id"},{"type":"text","text":", which PostHog’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sessions and web analytics group events by ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SessionKey"},{"type":"text","text":" is the UUIDv7 they require); a record"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with no session has none. The record’s vendor identifier and trace context, and any other"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"context value, aren’t sent."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Properties are read through the event’s schema in "},{"code":"plan","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", as "},{"code":"PropertyReader","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" reads them. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Sensitive","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" value is never sent, whatever the record reveals: the property is left"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"out, an element of an array is "},{"code":"null","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and one inside a type the plan can’t map is "},{"code":"null","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"property whose name starts with "},{"code":"$","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", which only a hand-written "},{"code":"Encodable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" conformance can"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"write, or is "},{"code":"distinct_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", is left out and logged at notice level, as PostHog reads those"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"names as settings ("},{"code":"$set","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"$process_person_profile","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":") or the identity."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"properties","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" also holds these members, for each of the keys the record’s context has a value"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for:"}]},{"type":"table","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Member","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Key"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Holds"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"$app_namespace","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"$app_version","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"$app_build","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ApplicationKey"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The bundle identifier, version and build, each left out when "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"$device_model","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"$device_type","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DeviceKey"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The model, and ","type":"text"},{"code":"Mobile","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"Tablet","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"Desktop","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"TV","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"Vision","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for the form factor; no ","type":"text"},{"code":"$device_type","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for a watch","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$locale"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LocaleKey"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The locale’s BCP 47 identifier, such as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"en-US"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"$network_wifi","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"$network_cellular","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NetworkKey"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Whether the connection is Wi-Fi, and whether it is cellular"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$os_name"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$os_version"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OperatingSystemKey"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The operating system’s name and version"}]}]]],"header":"row"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A record the encoder can’t write is left out of the request, and the batch’s other records are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sent: one whose event and version ","type":"text"},{"code":"plan","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" doesn’t describe, one whose event name starts with ","type":"text"},{"code":"$","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(a name PostHog keeps for its own events), one whose event isn’t ","type":"text"},{"code":"Encodable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", one that holds a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"value JSON can’t, and one too large for PostHog to store (","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogEncodingError","type":"reference"},{"text":").","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" returns them as ","type":"text"},{"code":"SkippedRecord","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"s, which ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" logs and reports","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"on its ","type":"text"},{"code":"dropReports","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" splits a batch into requests within the encoder’s limit, ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogBatchEncoder\/batchLimit","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"default, and makes none for a batch with no record it can write, so ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"text":" sends","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"nothing for it. PostHog answers a batch it takes with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"200, so ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"text":" retries one that gets no response, a 5xx, 408 or 429, and drops one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it rejects. A record sent again keeps its ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"uuid"},{"text":". The bytes are the same for the same records","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"on every run and platform: no whitespace, object members in the order of their names’ UTF-8","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"bytes.","type":"text"}]}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/posthogencoding\/posthogbatchencoder"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding"]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogBatchEncoder","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"metadata":{"title":"PostHogBatchEncoder","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"PostHogBatchEncoder"}],"role":"symbol","symbolKind":"struct","modules":[{"name":"PostHogEncoding"}],"roleHeading":"Structure","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"PostHogBatchEncoder"}],"externalID":"s:15PostHogEncoding0aB12BatchEncoderV","remo